Quaigh 0.0.6 ATPG: store each pattern's detected faults as a sparse list of
fault indices instead of one bool per fault (TestPatternGenerator::
pattern_detections). Patterns, detections and compaction are unchanged; only
memory changes. The dense table needed ~1.45 MB per pattern on the SoC's
1,449,256 faults and ran out of memory at 28 GB after ~20,000 patterns.
Checked (2026-11-24): on the core's scanned netlist (50,222 faults), seeds 1
and 7, stock and patched give byte-identical pattern files and result lines;
peak memory 1,004 -> 126 MB.

